{
  "email": "dana.whitfield@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender requests installing a free PDF editor from an external link. Checking account, department, and title for the software request process (KB-027)."
}

{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, I can't install the PDF editor from that link. Software that comes from a link in an email isn't installed by the help desk, because we can't verify the file is safe. Please don't open or run that download. Here's what to do instead: first, check the Company Portal (Software Center) on your laptop, since approved PDF editors may already be available there and you can install them yourself. If the one you want isn't listed, ask your manager to approve the request. After approval, the app goes through a security review and then gets installed. If you're unsure whether the vendor's email is legitimate, let us know and we can check it with the security team.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket from Dana Whitfield (CEO, VIP, user_id 1, device BL-LT-0101). Account active, not blocked, no failed logins, usual hours 08:00-18:00 ET. Request was to install http://free-pdf-tools.example/setup.exe, a file linked from a vendor email. Per KB-027, apps are not installed from email links and need manager approval plus security review if not in Company Portal. Declined the install and directed the user to Company Portal and the manager-approval path. I could not check Company Portal contents with my tools. No action queued. Note for technician: the link came from an unverified external vendor and the request is for an executable, so consider whether security should review the vendor email (KB-008) if Dana reports it or follows up.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-027"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
